          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em cosmic censorship hypothesis
            is the name of a pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjectures"} conjectures
            (
            %a{:href => "#Penrose69"}> Penrose 69
            ) saying that in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            must lie behind an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizon"} event horizon
          %p
            Both the weak and the strong form of the conjecture concern solutions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein%27s+equations"} Einstein's equations
            with physically realistic matter and generic compact or asymptotically flat initial data.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %strong strong cosmic censorship conjecture
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %strong weak cosmic censorship hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surface"} Cauchy development
            of a solution of Einstein’s equations with realistic matter possesses a complete future null infinity.
          %p Despite their names, the strong version does not necessarily imply the weak version.
          %p
            Without the ‘genericity’ condition, which needs to be carefully stated, both strong and weak cosmic censorship fail. That is, with carefully fine-tuned
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+value+problem"} initial data
            one can find counterexamples.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_the_weak_gravity_conjecture Relation to the weak gravity conjecture
          %p
            The weak cosmic censorship conjecture has many counterexamples in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \geq 5
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
            has argued that the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+gravity+conjecture"} weak gravity conjecture
            will save the cosmic censorship conjecture. The weak gravity conjecture says that in consistent theories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            the gravitational force exerted by any object (e.g. a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CrisfordSantos17"} Crisford-Santos 17
          %blockquote
            %p
              Subsequent calculations by Santos and Crisford supported Vafa’s hunch; the simulations they’re running now could verify that naked singularities become cloaked in black holes right at the point where gravity becomes the weakest force. (
              %a{:href => "https://www.quantamagazine.org/where-gravity-is-weak-and-naked-singularities-are-verboten-20170620/"}> Wolchover, June 20 2017
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+gravity+conjecture"} weak gravity conjecture
            was motivated from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+singularity+theorem"} Penrose singularity theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+gravity+conjecture"} weak gravity conjecture
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Penrose69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gravitational collapse: The role of general relativity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1016578408204"} doi:10.1023/A:1016578408204
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Penrose"}> Roger Penrose
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Question of Cosmic Censorship
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02702355"} doi:10.1007/BF02702355
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://adsabs.harvard.edu/full/1999JApA...20..233P"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"}> Klaas Landsman
                ,
                %em Singularities, black holes, and cosmic censorship: A tribute to Roger Penrose
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02687"}> arXiv:2101.02687
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmic_censorship_hypothesis"} Cosmic censorship hypothesis
          %h3#strong_cosmic_censorship Strong cosmic censorship
          %p For strong cosmic censorship, see:
          %ul
            %li
              Mihalis Dafermos,
              %em Strong cosmic censorship
              (
              %a{:href => "http://web.math.princeton.edu/~dafermos/research/structure-of-singularities/strong-cosmic-censorship.html"}> web
              )
          %p In 2017 Dafermos and Luk found a counterexample to strong cosmic censorship without the requirement that the initial data be generic:
          %ul
            %li
              Mihalis Dafermos and Jonathan Luk,
              %em
                The interior of dynamical vacuum black holes I: The
                = succeed "-stability" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^0
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.01722"}> arXiv:1710.01722
              )
          %p
            Discussion in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computability+in+physics"} computability in physics
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malament%E2%80%93Hogarth+spacetimes"} Malament–Hogarth spacetimes
          %ul
            %li#Etesi12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabor+Etesi"}> Gabor Etesi
              ,
              %em A proof of the Geroch-Horowitz-Penrose formulation of the strong cosmic censor conjecture motivated by computability theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1205.4550"}> arXiv:1205.4550
              )
          %p In 2020, Hod claimed a “remarkably compact proof” of strong cosmic censorship:
          %ul
            %li
              Shahar Hod,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A proof of the strong cosmic censorship conjecture
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.01449"} arXiv:2012.01449
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218271820420031"} doi:10.1142/S0218271820420031
          %h3#weak_cosmic_censorship Weak cosmic censorship
          %p Review of weak cosmic censorship:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"}> Robert Wald
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gravitational collapse and cosmic censorship
              = succeed "," do
                %em Black Holes, Gravitational Radiation and the Universe
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9710068"} arXiv:gr-qc/9710068
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-017-0934-7_5"} doi:10.1007/978-94-017-0934-7_5
          %p In 1993 Choptuik found a counterexample to weak cosmic censorship without the requirement that the initial data be generic, by considering a spherically symmetric solution of gravity coupled to a scalar field right on the brink of the formation of a black hole. This and subsequent work is reviewed here:
          %ul
            %li
              Carsten Gundlach,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Critical phenomena in gravitational collapse
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0001046"} arXiv:gr-qc/0001046
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.12942/lrr-2007-5"} doi:10.12942/lrr-2007-5
          %p For a proof of weak cosmic censorship in the spherically symmetric case, see:
          %ul
            %li
              Demetrios Christodoulou, The instability of naked singularities in the gravitational collapse of a scalar field,
              %em Ann. Math.
              149 (1999), 183-217. (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9901147"}> arxiv
              )
          %p
            A counterexample in 4-dimensional
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
          %ul
            %li#CrisfordSantos17
              Toby Crisford,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Santos"} Jorge Santos
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Violating weak cosmic censorship in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi AdS
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.05490"} arXiv:1702.05490
          %p A counterexample in 6-dimensional spacetime:
          %ul
            %li#AndradeFiguerasSperhake20
              Tomas Andrade, Pau Figueras, Ulrich Sperhake,
              %em Violations of Weak Cosmic Censorship in black hole collisions
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.03049"}> arXiv:2011.03049
              )
          %h3#more_references More references
          %p
            For
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BTZ+black+holes"} BTZ black holes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Emparan"}> Roberto Emparan
              , Marija Tomašević,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Strong cosmic censorship in the BTZ black hole
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.02083"} arXiv:2002.02083
          %p
            Relation to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+gravity+conjecture"} weak gravity conjecture
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Horowitz"}> Gary Horowitz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Santos"} Jorge Santos
              %em Further evidence for the weak gravity - cosmic censorship connection
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11096"}> arXiv:1901.11096
              )
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+corrections"} higher curvature corrections
          %ul
            %li
              Akash K Mishra, Sumanta Chakraborty,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Strong Cosmic Censorship in higher curvature gravity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.09855"} arXiv:1911.09855
        .revisedby
